  "question": {
    "text": "The antenna current of an AM transmitter is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> when only the carrier is sent, but it increases to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>93</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> when the carrier is modulated by a single sine wave. Find the percentage modulation."
  },
